%N A398366 Array read by ascending antidiagonals: A(n,k) = binomial(3*n-1+k,k).
%C A398366 A(n,k) is the number of possible states of a crystal of n atoms with k quanta constituting its energy in the Einstein model of a crystalline solid (see Callen on page 334).
%D A398366 Herbert B. Callen, Thermodynamics and an Introduction to the Thermostatistics, 2nd edition, John Wiley & Sons, Inc. (1985).
%F A398366 G.f.: (1 - y)^3/((1 - y)^3 - x).
%F A398366 E.g.f. of row n: hypergeom([3*n], [1], y).
%e A398366 The array begins:
%e A398366   1,  0,   0,    0,    0,     0,      0,      0, ...
%e A398366   1,  3,   6,   10,   15,    21,     28,     36, ...
